note tour-swap <name> <a> <b>: exchange two steps' places in the tour's list. The agent reaches for it to order siblings in layer and data tours, which have no call order the tool can derive (commit 8ba04f79ddad). Siblings in a tour are shown in list order, which for a flow follows the code's call order; layer and data tours have no call order, so this is how their author orders siblings. Parents are untouched, so swapping two steps under different parents changes only where each sits among its own siblings. Prints nothing on success.

